---
description: "Use when changing build scripts, filesystem paths, or platform-specific application behavior."
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "scripts/**"
  - "packages/electron/**"
  - ".gitattributes"
  - ".editorconfig"
---

# Cross-platform behavior

- Read supported runtime versions from `.nvmrc` and package manifests rather than assuming a version from this rule.
- Preserve file-name casing and repository line-ending settings; a path that works on macOS may fail on Linux.
- Use Node path utilities for filesystem paths and URL utilities for URLs. Do not apply filesystem joining to routes or HTTP addresses.
- Prefer portable Node/npm scripts for shared tasks. Existing platform-specific packaging/signing scripts may require a specific OS; label and preserve that boundary.
- Keep unsupported native capabilities explicit and safe. Test the affected platforms when available and disclose platform-specific validation gaps.
